      "message": "Do we need separate parallel directories for payload and metadata? The payload and bookkeeping allocations should remain separate so free payloads can be ASan-poisoned, but their pointers could share one subpool descriptor:\n\n```c\ntypedef struct\n{\n  u8 *pool;\n  u8 *slot_state;\n  u32 *next_free;\n} vlib_pool_cache_subpool_t;\n\nvlib_pool_cache_subpool_t **subpool_chunks;\n```\n\nLookup could then resolve the subpool once:\n\n```c\nsp \u003d pool_cache_subpool_at (c, pidx);\nstate \u003d sp-\u003eslot_state[eidx];\nelt \u003d sp-\u003epool + (uword) eidx * c-\u003eelt_size;\n```\n\nThis preserves separate payload/metadata storage while removing one directory and the need to keep two directory entries synchronized.",
