      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems to bring back the pointer-chasing per-thread representation discussed on an earlier patchset. Could we compare it with fixed backing pools plus bounded per-thread index stacks? Each backing pool would be permanently fixed-size, so its payload pointers remain stable, and its native freelist would only serve as the locked global depot.\n\nThe common path would be a contiguous stack push/pop:\n\n```c\nalloc (c):\n  pt \u003d \u0026c-\u003eper_thread[thread_index]\n  if (pt-\u003elen \u003d\u003d 0)\n    refill (c, pt)\n  index \u003d pt-\u003eindices[--pt-\u003elen]\n  slot_state[index] \u003d ALLOCATED\n  return index\n\nfree (c, index):\n  if (!CAS (slot_state[index], ALLOCATED, FREE))\n    reject_double_free ()\n  pt \u003d \u0026c-\u003eper_thread[thread_index]\n  pt-\u003eindices[pt-\u003elen++] \u003d index\n  if (pt-\u003elen \u003e 2 * c-\u003ebatch_size)\n    flush (c, pt)\n```\n\nThe slow paths would transfer batches through the backing pools:\n\n```c\nrefill (c, pt):\n  lock (c)\n  while (pt-\u003elen \u003c c-\u003ebatch_size):\n    sp \u003d find_subpool_with_free_elements (c)\n    if (sp \u003d\u003d NULL)\n      sp \u003d add_fixed_subpool (c)\n    eidx \u003d pool_get_index (sp-\u003epool)\n    pt-\u003eindices[pt-\u003elen++] \u003d encode (sp-\u003eindex, eidx)\n  unlock (c)\n\nflush (c, pt):\n  lock (c)\n  while (pt-\u003elen \u003e c-\u003ebatch_size):\n    index \u003d pt-\u003eindices[--pt-\u003elen]\n    sp \u003d subpool (index)\n    pool_put_index (sp-\u003epool, element (index))\n  unlock (c)\n```\n\n`slot_state` would still be required because an index held in a thread cache appears allocated to the backing pool despite being logically free. If type-erased pool integration proves too complicated, bounded local stacks may still be useful with the existing fixed payload chunks. This seems worth comparing for steady-state and refill/growth performance.",
      "revId": "53db9de5a6031b8973e9c3e5b681829dd2adb9d9",
      "serverId": "6d2eb258-4fe2-443e-8a38-ca81da23d4c2"
    },
