      "side": 1,
      "message": "Could we organize this as two explicit cache lines? `clib_spinlock_t` is only an 8-byte pointer—the lock object itself is separately cache-line aligned—but the current layout mixes fields read by every allocation/free with counters modified during refill and flush.\n\nFor example:\n\n```c\ntypedef struct vlib_pool_cache_t_\n{\n  CLIB_CACHE_LINE_ALIGN_MARK (hot);\n  vlib_pool_cache_thread_t *per_thread;\n  vlib_pool_cache_subpool_meta_t **subpool_meta_chunks;\n  u8 ***pool_chunks;\n  uword elt_size;\n  u32 log2_subpool_size;\n  u32 subpool_size;\n  u32 subpool_mask;\n  u32 max_subpools;\n  u32 max_subpool_chunks;\n  u32 n_subpools;\n  u32 batch_size;\n  u32 align;\n\n  CLIB_CACHE_LINE_ALIGN_MARK (slow);\n  clib_spinlock_t lock;\n  u32 global_free_list;\n  u32 n_global_free;\n  u64 global_lock_acquisitions;\n  u64 growths;\n  char *name;\n  format_function_t *format_element;\n  struct vlib_pool_cache_t_ *next_instance;\n} vlib_pool_cache_t;\n```\n\nThis should keep the common path on one read-mostly line and isolate the locked mutable state. The resulting structure would be about 128 bytes.",
      "revId": "53db9de5a6031b8973e9c3e5b681829dd2adb9d9",
